  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Pointing at things",
   "md": "[[این|in|this]] is for things near you, [[آن|ān|that]] for things further away – spoken *un*. Both work as a word on their own ([[این چیست؟|in chist?|what is this?]]) and in front of a noun ([[این کتاب|in ketāb|this book]]). The plurals are [[این‌ها|in-hā|these]] and [[آن‌ها|ān-hā|those]] – the same *ān-hā* you learned for *they*.\n\nFor places, use [[اینجا|injā|here]] and [[آنجا|ānjā|there]].\n\nThe useful question [[یعنی چه؟|ya'ni che?|what does it mean?]] and the word [[یعنی|ya'ni|it means]] will carry you through many conversations: *«ketāb» ya'ni book*. To ask for the English word, say [[به انگلیسی چه می‌شود؟|be engelisi che mi-shavad?|what does it become in English?]]."
  },
