  {
   "type": "grammar",
   "title": "Plurals: add -hā",
   "md": "To make almost any noun plural, add [[ها|-hā]]: [[کتاب|ketāb]] → [[کتاب‌ها|ketāb-hā|books]], [[میز|miz]] → [[میزها|miz-hā|tables]]. In careful writing, *-hā* is kept slightly apart from the word with the zero-width joiner, so the letters do not run together: کتاب‌ها.\n\nTwo things make Persian plurals easy. After a number you **do not** use the plural: [[دو پنجره|do panjare|two windows]], [[سه کتاب|se ketāb|three books]]. And a plural subject that is not a person usually takes a **singular** verb in formal Persian: [[این‌ها مداد هستند|in-hā medād hastand]] is fine in speech, but you will also read [[کتاب‌ها روی میز است|ketāb-hā ru-ye miz ast|the books are on the table]].",
