  {
   "type": "grammar",
   "title": "'A book' and 'the book'",
   "md": "Persian has no word for *the*. A bare noun is definite or general from context: [[کتاب روی میز است|ketāb ru-ye miz ast|the book is on the table]].\n\nTo say *a* …, either put [[یک|yek|one]] before the noun, or add [[ی|-i]] to the end, or both: [[یک کتاب|yek ketāb]], [[کتابی|ketāb-i]], [[یک کتابی|yek ketāb-i]] all mean *a book*. In speech *yek* is usually *ye*: [[یه کتاب|ye ketāb]].\n\nAfter a vowel the ending needs a *y*: [[خانه‌ای|khāne-i|a house]] (written with a separate ای), [[دانشجویی|dāneshju-yi|a student]].",
   "examples": [
    {
     "fa": "این یک کتاب است.",
     "r": "in yek ketāb ast.",
     "en": "This is a book.",
     "col": "این یه کتابه.",
