  {
   "type": "grammar",
   "title": "The ezafe: linking words together",
   "md": "The **ezafe** ([[اضافه|ezāfe|addition]]) is an unstressed **-e** that links a noun to whatever describes or owns it. The owner or description comes **after** the noun: [[کتاب سارا|ketāb-e Sārā|Sara's book]], [[کیف آقای کریمی|kif-e āghā-ye Karimi|Mr Karimi's bag]], [[کلاس ما|kelās-e mā|our class]], [[کتاب فارسی|ketāb-e fārsi|a Persian book]].\n\nAfter a consonant the ezafe is **not written** – you simply say it. After a vowel it is written as [[ی|-ye]]: [[خانه‌ی سارا|khāne-ye Sārā|Sara's house]], [[آقای کریمی|āghā-ye Karimi|Mr Karimi]], [[دانشجوی خوب|dāneshju-ye khub|a good student]].\n\nLinks can chain: [[کلید در کلاس ما|kelid-e dar-e kelās-e mā|the key of the door of our classroom]].",
